    "status": "present",
    "value": "The text now arrives as a sequence of chunks. After each chunk you must output the text that is definitely safe to release: text that comes before any stop word occurrence. Stop as soon as a stop word is certainly found (no earlier position could still start one) and release only the text before it. Otherwise hold back the shortest suffix that could still be the beginning of a stop word, and release everything before it. Return one string per chunk plus a final string for the end of the stream (which releases anything held back, cut at a stop word if one is present). After a stop, all later outputs are empty. Joined together, the outputs equal the variant-1 answer for the concatenated text."
  },
